{"text": "This is M4’s plan plane, with the cart at rest at seven metres, three metres from the wall. The best plan is the corner where both motor limits meet. The active-set method guesses which limits hold: none, then the first motor limit, then both. Two changes, and it lands exactly on the corner. The interior-point method starts inside the polygon and takes Newton steps along a curve that never leaves it; each step builds and factors a new matrix. ADMM, the method inside OSQP, takes many small steps. Each one reuses the same matrix, so it is cheap, but it only gets close, to a tolerance.", "lang": "en", "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural", "duration": 40.688, "words": [[0.1, 0.35, "This"], [0.35, 0.537, "is"], [0.662, 1.325, "M4’s"], [1.337, 1.712, "plan"], [1.725, 2.163, "plane"], [2.562, 2.663, "with"], [2.663, 2.75, "the"], [2.75, 3.075, "cart"], [3.075, 3.238, "at"], [3.237, 3.562, "rest"], [3.562, 3.625, "at"], [3.625, 4.013, "seven"], [4.013, 4.525, "metres"], [4.7, 5.075, "three"], [5.075, 5.45, "metres"], [5.45, 5.562, "from"], [5.562, 5.625, "the"], [5.638, 5.975, "wall"], [6.375, 6.438, "The"], [6.45, 6.7, "best"], [6.7, 6.987, "plan"], [6.987, 7.062, "is"], [7.075, 7.163, "the"], [7.162, 7.625, "corner"], [7.775, 8.0, "where"], [8.012, 8.35, "both"], [8.35, 8.662, "motor"], [8.662, 8.925, "limits"], [8.938, 9.275, "meet"], [9.688, 9.787, "The"], [9.8, 10.463, "active-set"], [10.463, 11.0, "method"], [11.188, 11.662, "guesses"], [11.675, 11.9, "which"], [11.9, 12.225, "limits"], [12.225, 12.55, "hold"], [13.15, 13.537, "none"], [14.012, 14.112, "then"], [14.113, 14.188, "the"], [14.188, 14.525, "first"], [14.537, 14.825, "motor"], [14.825, 15.112, "limit"], [15.325, 15.537, "then"], [15.55, 16.088, "both"], [16.488, 16.663, "Two"], [16.663, 17.363, "changes"], [17.575, 17.675, "and"], [17.675, 17.775, "it"], [17.775, 18.137, "lands"], [18.15, 18.825, "exactly"], [18.837, 18.925, "on"], [18.925, 18.988, "the"], [19.0, 19.462, "corner"], [19.863, 